SUMMARY:Deadline: University of Notre Dame: Love Ethic Social Innovator Fel
 lowships 2028 (residency plus USD 15\,000 and up to USD 50\,000 project fu
 nding)
DESCRIPTION:Up to six short-term fellowships for practitioners outside acad
 emia (nonprofit leaders\, community organisers\, social workers\, faith le
 aders\, entrepreneurs\, public-sector professionals) who want time and spa
 ce to design a new initiative grounded in love-based ethics. Funded by the
  John Templeton Foundation.\n\nOrganisation: University of Notre Dame\, In
 stitute for Ethics and the Common Good\nLocation: Notre Dame\, Indiana\, U
 SA. In person: one-week workshop in October 2027 and four-week residency i
 n February 2028.\nAward: Stipend for housing during the residency plus rel
 ocation support\; USD 15\,000 to the fellow's organisation to offset the f
 our-week sabbatical\; up to USD 50\,000 in subgrant funding after the resi
 dency to pilot the proposed project\; travel to all programme gatherings c
 overed. No application fee.\nDuration: Workshop October 2027 (one week)\; 
 residency February 2028 (four weeks)\; ongoing network convenings.\n\nMore
 : https://ethics.nd.edu/fellowships-and-grants/social-innovator-fellowship
 s/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ethics.nd.edu/fellowships-and-grants/social-innovator-fellowshi
 ps/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Notre Dame\, Indiana\, USA. In person: one-week workshop in Octobe
 r 2027 and four-week residency in February 2028.
END:VEVENT
