UID:art-explora-cite-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T002447Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261031
SUMMARY:Deadline: Art Explora x Cité internationale des arts Residency\, 7
 th Call (Paris)
DESCRIPTION:The 7th call of the Art Explora residency programme at the Cit
 é internationale des arts opened 21 September 2026. The programme support
 s projects exploring the crossovers of art with science\, technology and e
 cology\, which makes it one of the stronger art-science fits in Europe.\n\
 nOrganisation: Art Explora Foundation and Cité internationale des arts\nL
 ocation: Paris\, France. Open worldwide to artists with at least 5 years o
 f professional practice.\nAward: EUR 1\,000 per month living stipend plus 
 up to EUR 3\,000 production grant\, a furnished live-work studio of around
  50 m2 at the Cité internationale des arts\, round-trip travel to Paris a
 nd curatorial mentoring. No application fee.\nDuration: 3- or 6-month resi
 dencies during 2027\; 3 months for duos (artist plus researcher\, curator 
 or writer).\n\nMore: https://artexplora.plateformecandidature.com/?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://artexplora.plateformecandidature.com/?utm_source=artificialnouv
 eaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Paris\, France. Open worldwide to artists with at least 5 years of
  professional practice.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:eyebeam-agency-nyc-residency-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T002447Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261115
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
SUMMARY:Deadline: Eyebeam AGENCY NYC Residency\, Spring 2027
DESCRIPTION:The NYC track of Eyebeam's AGENCY residency cycle supports New 
 York City-based artists exploring questions of agency at a moment when AI 
 systems increasingly act\, decide and carry out tasks on our behalf: how t
 o preserve human agency as these systems shape human behavior\, how to ass
 ert agency in imagining and building the societies we inhabit\, and what a
 gency becomes when understood as...\n\nOrganisation: Eyebeam\nLocation: Ne
 w York City\, USA. Applicants must live within the five boroughs and be ab
 le to work on site at Eyebeam at least one day a week for the full residen
 cy term (15 March to 11 June 2027).\nAward: USD 5\,000 stipend per selecte
 d artist\, plus mentorship and access to tools and technical expertise thr
 ough Eyebeam's network. No application fee (via Submittable).\nDuration: 1
 5 March to 11 June 2027\; on site at Eyebeam at least one day per week.\n\
 nMore: https://eyebeam.org/articles/agency-nyc-residency?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://eyebeam.org/articles/agency-nyc-residency?utm_source=artificial
 nouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New York City\, USA. Applicants must live within the five boroughs
  and be able to work on site at Eyebeam at least one day a week for the fu
 ll residency term (15 March to 11 June 2027).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rome-prize-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261111T002447Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261101
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261102
SUMMARY:Deadline: American Academy in Rome: Rome Prize Fellowship 2027-28
DESCRIPTION:The Rome Prize supports roughly 30 artists and scholars a year 
 with a residential fellowship at the American Academy in Rome\; discipline
 s include Design and Visual Arts\, where media and new-genre work is regul
 arly funded. Fellows receive a USD 16\,000 (half-term) or USD 30\,000 (ful
 l-term) stipend plus housing\, workspace and weekday meals on the Academy'
 s Janiculum campus.\n\nOrganisation: American Academy in Rome\nLocation: R
 ome\, Italy (residential fellowship at the Academy\; US organisation with 
 NYC office). RESTRICTED: US citizens for most categories\; foreign nationa
 ls resident in the US for the 3 years preceding the deadline may apply onl
 y in certain categories.\nAward: Stipends of USD 16\,000 (half-term\, abou
 t 5 months) and USD 30\,000 (full-term\, about 10 months)\, plus housing\,
  workspace and weekday meals. Approximately 30 fellowships per year. APPLI
 CATION FEE: USD 50 by 1 November (USD 60 for multiple categories)\; USD 80
 /90 in the late window to 15 November.\nDuration: 5 or 10 months\n\nMore: 
 https://www.aarome.org/apply/rome-prize?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.aarome.org/apply/rome-prize?utm_source=artificialnouveaugra
 ntdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Rome\, Italy (residential fellowship at the Academy\; US organisat
 ion with NYC office). RESTRICTED: US citizens for most categories\; foreig
 n nationals resident in the US for the 3 years preceding the deadline may 
 apply only in certain categories.
END:VEVENT
